  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception and actuation: G1 encodes the robot's sensor outcomes (obstacle and clear events), G2 encodes the robot's motion commands. The specification automata E1 and E2 enforce safe, coverage-oriented exploration: E1 binds each perception state to a unique, safe action, preferring random_walk in clear, rotate_clockwise for front/left obstacles, rotate_counterclockwise for right obstacles, and full_rotate only as a last-resort. E2 prevents repeated identical actions and ensures alternation between random_walk and move_forward for coverage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and actuation into distinct plant automata for modularity.",
